menu "Infineon DAP probe"

    config AEL_DAP_BRINGUP_AT_BOOT
        bool "Run the DAP bring-up checkpoints at boot"
        default n
        help
            Runs the documented DAP bring-up sequence once at startup and logs
            each checkpoint with its expected value: sync drawing 0xAAAAAAAA,
            the DAPISC read, client_set, and CLIENT_ID reading 0x0260.

            Off by default because it drives Port C, which Black Magic Probe
            also uses.  Enable it while bringing a target up, then turn it off.

    config AEL_DAP_BRINGUP_CLOCK_HZ
        int "Bring-up bit rate (Hz)"
        depends on AEL_DAP_BRINGUP_AT_BOOT
        default 1000000
        range 100000 4000000
        help
            Deliberately slow so a scope can follow it. The bit-banged PHY will
            not reach much past 2 MHz; the GP-SPI path is what goes faster.

endmenu
